'''Charles Michael Patrick''' (September 6, 1952 – April 27, 2008) was an American professional [[American football|football]] player who was a [[Punter (American football)|punter]] for the [[New England Patriots]] of the [[National Football League]] (NFL) from 1975 to 1978. He was born in [[Austin, Texas]], and graduated from [[Biloxi High School]] in [[Biloxi, Mississippi]]. He played [[college football]] for the [[Mississippi State Bulldogs football|Mississippi State Bulldogs]]. He died at age 55 in Biloxi.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://news.yahoo.com/s/cpress/20080429/ca_pr_on_fo/obit_nfl_pats_patrick_1 |title=Former New England Patriots punter Mike Patrick dies at age 55 |accessdate=2008-04-30 |date=2008-04-28 |publisher=Associated Press via Yahoo! News |archive-date=2020-05-26 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200526045019/https://news.yahoo.com/s/cpress/20080429/ca_pr_on_fo/obit_nfl_pats_patrick_1 |url-status=dead }}</ref>
